  <reporting-org ref="XM-DAC-7" type="10">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Ministry of Foreign Affairs of the Netherlands</narrative>
  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Regional Advisory (RAG) Group 2026 - Eswatini from 24 to 28 of August 2026.</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Regional Advisory Group is an annual meeting that brings together implementing partners, namely (UNFPA, UNDP, IOM, Aidsfonds, Frontline Aids and Young Africa) and the Embassies (EKN LUA, EKN PRE, EKN HAR and EKN MAP) to jointly reflect on the challenges, successes, and lessons learned from the SRHR regional  programme during the previous year of implementation and jointly make agreements of improvements for the coming year. 

For 2026, the selected host country is the Kingdom of Eswatini. This year will also include the participation of implementing partners from the new HIV programme. As such, the gathering will not only serve as a moment for reflection, but also as an opportunity to pass the baton and legacy to the new partners. It will provide a space to share lessons learned, successes, and challenges, while also identifying approaches, practices, and experiences that can inform the implementation of the new HIV instrument.

The event will take place from 24 to 28 August 2026. The first two days will be dedicated to field visits, followed by two and a half days of conference sessions, including discussions among partners and the Embassies.

On the first evening of the conference component, a reception will be hosted for participants. The reception will also include high-level guests from Eswatini, who may include the Minister of Health, the Commissioner for Human Rights, the Minister of Youth, the UN Resident Coordinator, and heads of UN agencies based in the country.</narrative>
  </description>
